--- !u!114 &910819586
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 910819585}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: aa92709839b4cd64e8bd442d4c4ab700, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: ConveyorSystem.Demo::ConveyorSystem.Demo.TutorialController
  Steps:
  - Title: Welcome to the Modular Conveyor Belt System
    Body: 'This tutorial walks through every part of the system, one live example
      at a time.


      A conveyor line is built from <b>modules</b>. You place
      them next to each other and they <b>connect by themselves</b> - no manager
      object, no manual wiring.


      On the right you see all 10 modules. <color=#5CFF8A>Green
      arrows</color> show where parcels enter, <color=#FFA040>orange arrows</color>
      where they leave.'
    Task: 
    Code: 
    Focus: {fileID: 1152531242}
    Distance: 13
    Pitch: 44
    Yaw: -10
    Actions: []
  - Title: Parcels
    Body: 'Anything that travels on a belt is a <b>Parcel</b>: a GameObject with
      the <b>Parcel</b> component (plus a collider and, optionally, a Rigidbody).


      Each
      parcel carries data you can route on:

      - <b>Type</b>: Generic, Fragile,
      Heavy, Perishable

      - <b>Size</b>: Small, Medium, Large

      - <b>Weight</b>
      in kg


      The <b>PlayerInteraction</b> component lets the player pick parcels
      up, put them on a belt or drop them.'
    Task: Click a parcel on the table to pick it up, then click the belt to put it
      on. Right-click drops it.
    Code: 
    Focus: {fileID: 1195722142}
    Distance: 9
    Pitch: 44
    Yaw: -10
    Actions:
    - {fileID: 1249063110}
  - Title: The Straight Conveyor
    Body: 'Every module moves a parcel through three points:


      <color=#5CFF8A><b>Input</b></color>
      - where the parcel enters

      <b>Center</b> - where the module decides where
      it goes next

      <color=#FFA040><b>Output</b></color> - where it is handed
      to the next module


      A module holds <b>one parcel at a time</b>. The
      <b>Speed</b> field sets units per second.


      This line starts at a <b>Source</b>
      (an Unloader with endless parcels) and ends in a <b>Sink</b> (a Loader that
      removes them).'
    Task: 
    Code: 
    Focus: {fileID: 460409621}
    Distance: 10.5
    Pitch: 44
    Yaw: -10
    Actions: []
  - Title: Automatic Connections
    Body: 'Each module has child trigger colliders with a <b>ConveyorTrigger</b>
      component: one on the input (<b>Is Output</b> off) and one per exit (<b>Is
      Output</b> on, with an <b>Output Index</b>).


      When an output trigger
      overlaps another module''s input trigger, the two connect. Move them apart
      and they disconnect - even during Play.


      Watch the gap: parcels wait
      in front of it until the missing piece arrives.'
    Task: Go back and forth with Left / Right to replay the missing piece sliding
      in.
    Code: 
    Focus: {fileID: 21266419}
    Distance: 10.5
    Pitch: 44
    Yaw: -10
    Actions:
    - {fileID: 756660572}
  - Title: Back-pressure & the Pauser
    Body: 'If the next module is busy, a parcel <b>waits at the center</b>. Blocked
      lines back up one module at a time - no parcel is ever lost.


      Waiting
      is <b>event-driven</b>: a waiting module costs nothing per frame and wakes
      up as soon as the module in front frees up.


      The <b>Pauser</b> holds
      every parcel for <b>Pause Duration</b> seconds and can be stopped completely
      with <b>IsActive</b>.'
    Task: Press <b>Space</b> to start the stopped Pauser. Press it again to stop
      it and watch the line back up.
    Code: "// Stop and start a Pauser from your own code or a UI button\npauser.StopConveyor();\npauser.StartConveyor();\npauser.ToggleConveyor();\n\n//
      React to it\npauser.ActiveChanged += (p, active) =>\n    Debug.Log(active ?
      \"running\" : \"stopped\");"
    Focus: {fileID: 238871659}
    Distance: 12.5
    Pitch: 44
    Yaw: -10
    Actions:
    - {fileID: 1127702717}
  - Title: Corners
    Body: '<b>CornerConveyor</b> turns right, <b>CornerConveyorLeft</b> turns left.
      The parcel rotates in place at the center (<b>Rotation Speed</b>) and then
      leaves through the side.


      The example combines both to make an S-shaped
      line.'
    Task: 
    Code: 
    Focus: {fileID: 1280842124}
    Distance: 10.5
    Pitch: 44
    Yaw: -10
    Actions: []
  - Title: Splitter
    Body: 'The <b>Splitter</b> has two outputs and sends parcels to them <b>round-robin</b>:
      one left, one right. If one side is blocked, the other side keeps getting parcels.


      Use
      it to spread load over parallel lines. The counters above the sinks show the
      even split.'
    Task: 
    Code: 
    Focus: {fileID: 1258825660}
    Distance: 10.5
    Pitch: 44
    Yaw: -10
    Actions: []
  - Title: Smart Splitter
    Body: 'The <b>Smart Splitter</b> routes by <b>parcel type</b>. <b>Type To Output</b>
      maps each type (Generic, Fragile, Heavy, Perishable) to an output index; unmapped
      types use <b>Default Output Index</b>.


      Here Fragile and Perishable
      go to <b>Express</b>, Generic and Heavy to <b>Standard</b>.


      With <b>Strict
      Routing</b> on, a parcel waits for its own lane instead of taking a free one.'
    Task: 
    Code: 'smartSplitter.TypeToOutput = new[] { 1, 0, 1, 0 };

      //                                
      G  F  H  P

      smartSplitter.DefaultOutputIndex = 1;

      smartSplitter.StrictRouting
      = true;'
    Focus: {fileID: 317833976}
    Distance: 12.5
    Pitch: 44
    Yaw: -10
    Actions: []
  - Title: Joiner & Multi-Joiner
    Body: 'A <b>Joiner</b> merges two lines into one. It holds one parcel at a time,
      so the input lines take turns.


      A <b>Multi-Joiner</b> accepts parcels
      into a <b>FIFO queue</b> (<b>Queue Capacity</b>), so busy input lines keep
      moving instead of waiting.'
    Task: 
    Code: 
    Focus: {fileID: 1183646950}
    Distance: 11.5
    Pitch: 44
    Yaw: -10
    Actions: []
  - Title: Loader, Unloader & Storage
    Body: 'A <b>ParcelStorage</b> keeps parcels out of the scene (deactivated) until
      they are needed.


      The <b>Unloader</b> takes parcels out of a storage
      and starts them on the line. The <b>Loader</b> puts them back in. While the
      storage is full, the Loader stops accepting parcels, so the line backs up instead
      of losing them.


      Together they make a closed loop that runs forever.'
    Task: 
    Code: '// Fill a storage from code

      storage.StoreParcel(Instantiate(parcelPrefab));


      //
      Parcels placed under StorageRoot in the scene

      // are picked up automatically
      on start.


      // Watch it

      storage.ParcelStored += (s, p) => count++;

      storage.Changed
      += s => label.text = s.Count.ToString();'
    Focus: {fileID: 1055187744}
    Distance: 12.5
    Pitch: 44
    Yaw: -10
    Actions: []
  - Title: Events
    Body: 'Every module raises events: <b>ParcelEntered</b>, <b>ParcelExited</b>,
      <b>ParcelBlocked</b>, <b>ParcelRouted</b> and <b>AvailabilityChanged</b>. Storages
      raise <b>ParcelStored</b> and <b>ParcelRetrieved</b>.


      No code needed:
      the <b>ConveyorEvents</b> component exposes them as UnityEvents. Here its <b>OnParcelEntered</b>
      is wired to the lamp''s <b>Flash</b> method in the Inspector - every parcel
      on the watched belt flashes the lamp.'
    Task: Exit Play mode, select <b>Watched Belt</b> in Station 10 and look at the
      <b>Conveyor Events</b> component.
    Code: "using ConveyorSystem;\nusing UnityEngine;\n\npublic class DeliveryCounter
      : MonoBehaviour\n{\n    public ConveyorBase loader;\n    int delivered;\n\n   
      void OnEnable()  => loader.ParcelExited += OnExited;\n    void OnDisable()
      => loader.ParcelExited -= OnExited;\n\n    void OnExited(ConveyorBase c, Parcel
      p)\n    {\n        delivered++;\n        Debug.Log($\"{p.Type} delivered ({delivered})\");\n   
      }\n}"
    Focus: {fileID: 582534753}
    Distance: 12.5
    Pitch: 44
    Yaw: -10
    Actions: []
  - Title: Editor Tools
    Body: 'Building lines in the editor is fast:


      <b>Auto Snap</b> - drop
      a module near another and it snaps onto the nearest connector, turned to continue
      the flow.

      <b>Connection overlay</b> - green = connected, orange = close
      but not connected, red = open exit.

      <b>Validate Scene</b> - finds setup
      mistakes and links to the object.


      Everything is under <b>Tools > Conveyor
      System</b>. In this example ''Drag Me'' is not connected, so parcels stop in
      front of it.'
    Task: 'Exit Play mode, drag <b>Drag Me</b> (Station 11) a little and release:
      it snaps into place. Then run <b>Tools > Conveyor System > Validate Scene</b>.'
    Code: 
    Focus: {fileID: 1382294929}
    Distance: 10.5
    Pitch: 44
    Yaw: -10
    Actions: []
  - Title: Write Your Own Module
    Body: 'Every module derives from <b>ConveyorBase</b>. Most custom behaviour is
      one override:


      <b>GetNextConveyor(parcel)</b> - choose the next module,
      or return null to wait.

      <b>MoveParcelRoutine(parcel)</b> - full control
      over movement.


      To wait in a custom routine, <b>yield return WaitForChange</b>
      - the routine sleeps at no cost until something changes.'
    Task: 
    Code: "using ConveyorSystem;\n\n// Heavy parcels (>= 10 kg) go left, the rest
      right\npublic class WeightSplitter : ConveyorBase\n{\n    public float HeavyThreshold
      = 10f;\n\n    public override ConveyorBase GetNextConveyor(Parcel parcel)\n   
      {\n        int lane = parcel.Weight >= HeavyThreshold ? 0 : 1;\n        foreach
      (var next in NextConveyors[lane])\n            if (next != null && next.CanAcceptParcel())\n               
      return next;\n\n        return null; // wait at the center\n    }\n}"
    Focus: {fileID: 1593328951}
    Distance: 12.5
    Pitch: 44
    Yaw: -10
    Actions: []
  - Title: You're Ready!
    Body: 'You have seen every part of the system.


      Next steps:

      - <b>Demo.unity</b>
      - a complete sorting facility that runs by itself

      - <b>Sandbox.unity</b>
      - build your own lines in Play mode

      - <b>Documentation.pdf</b> -
      setup guide and full API reference


      Start a new line by dragging the
      prefabs from <b>Conveyor System/Prefab</b> into your scene.'
    Task: 
    Code: 
    Focus: {fileID: 1152531242}
    Distance: 15
    Pitch: 44
    Yaw: -10
    Actions: []
